s  come to work here in startups  and to work in tech companies not only  reflects the high  quality internet of lisbon but it also  is  because of the talent drawn here  from across the world and the quality of  training  from specialized university in braga  porto  or here in lisbon and this bodes  well for portugal it bodes well for the  european  digital decade we have ahead of us  to build on this and this is the  foundation can start on  and where portugal has a head start to  build on this  we need to invest now for example in  skills  skills and smes digitalize smes in data  make sure we have a data economy we  should use our industrial data  at the moment being eighty percent of  the industrial data we collect on an  everyday basis  are never ever used once what a waste so  let's use it together  artificial intelligence human centered  artificial intelligence  5g infrastructure and we need to ensure  that the high-speed internet of lisbon  is available  everywhere in rural areas like marvao  or mansaras everywhere  so this is an example of how  next generation eu can help build  a better world to live in  and nowhere is this  more important for portugal  europe and the world  than when it comes to our environment  portugal is at the front line  in the fight against climate change you  know it all  i don't have to tell you this country is  sadly enough used to forest fires  but it has been used to these forest  fires for years  the difference now is that the frequency  and the intensity has increased and you  know  all know that the extreme weather  situations the frequency  and the intensity has increased and this  is only the beginning of climate change  there is an urgent need to act  and the pandemic has only made that more  urgent  but it's not only an urgent need to act  there's also a huge opportunity in it  that goes with it for portugal and all  those who invest  early in the green transition of today  because if we're going to be successful  in fighting climate change  if the world will follow the european  example  portugal and europe will be at the front  line  will be the exporter of technology of  knowledge of  innovation because we will need those  new those clean technologies  so this is what the european green deal  is all about  have a different economy am a  sustainable economy a circular economy  but also be innovative and be at the  forefront  of prosperity and growth that is a  different growth  that's a growth that gives back  more to the planet than it takes away  from planet  and this european green deal is our  blueprint  for the transformation of our economy  and our society  for the good of the planet  for the good of people and  for the good of our long-term prosperity  the core ambition is for europe to be a  climate neutral continent  by 2050. this is an ambition long-term  goal that needs short-term action  now and this is why  earlier this month the commission  announced a new target for emission  reductions of at least 55  by 2030 this  goal this road map  will give certainty and direction  that investors need that entrepreneurs  need innovators need they need the  certainty  they need the clear direction here in  portugal and across europe  and now we have with next generation eu  the investment into that clear direction  and that certainty we have the plan we  have the road map  and we have the investment  from investing in high-speed train  connections for example  to building renovations  as you know forty percent of our co2  emissions are coming from buildings  so insulate them renovate them  make them more efficient the investment  is here  clean mobility hydrogen  you name it next generation  you will invest in projects that make  the biggest  difference for each country  and portugal has always  been a front runner in the transition  towards cleaner energy  you started your clean transition back  in 2005  and today more than half of portugal's  electricity needs are now met by 